# Mapping helper: Railway MySQL / Redis plugin vars → BE env
# Exact variable names can differ by Railway template — check dashboard.

# Typical Railway MySQL:
#   MYSQLHOST, MYSQLPORT, MYSQLUSER, MYSQLPASSWORD, MYSQLDATABASE
#   or MYSQL_URL
#
# Map to BE:
#   MYSQL_HOST       ← MYSQLHOST (private)
#   MYSQL_PORT       ← MYSQLPORT
#   MYSQL_SCHEMA     ← MYSQLDATABASE  (create db_clinic if empty)
#   MYSQL_ROOT_USERNAME ← MYSQLUSER
#   MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD ← MYSQLPASSWORD

# Typical Railway Redis:
#   REDISHOST, REDISPORT, REDISPASSWORD, REDISUSER
#   or REDIS_URL
#
# Map to BE:
#   REDIS_HOST     ← REDISHOST
#   REDIS_PORT     ← REDISPORT
#   REDIS_PASSWORD ← REDISPASSWORD
#   REDIS_USERNAME ← REDISUSER (if any)

# Tip: In Railway, use "Variable Reference" / shared variables between services
# so BE auto-picks MySQL + Redis private hostnames.
